  "charterIntro": "e-Himaya is the national platform for reporting emergencies to the Civil Protection. Before using it, please read how your data is handled and what your obligations are.",
  "charterDataTitle": "Data we collect and why",
  "charterDataBody": "For each report: its category, your description, the position of the incident and the photos, videos or voice messages you attach. If you create an account: your name, national ID card (CIN) number, phone number and region. This data is used only to handle emergencies and to inform you of the follow-up of your reports.",
  "charterLawTitle": "Legal framework",
  "charterLawBody": "Your personal data is processed in accordance with Organic Law No. 2004-63 of 27 July 2004 on the protection of personal data and its implementing texts, under the supervision of the National Authority for the Protection of Personal Data (INPDP).",
  "charterAnonymousTitle": "Reporting without an account",
  "charterAnonymousBody": "You may report without an account. The app then uses a random key created on this phone; the platform keeps only a pseudonym derived from it and does not store your IP address. Anonymous reporting from a device can be suspended after confirmed false reports.",
  "charterRightsTitle": "Your rights",
  "charterRightsBody": "You have the right to access, rectify and object to the processing of your data under the conditions set by law. You can exercise these rights with the platform operator and refer the matter to the INPDP.",
  "charterRetentionTitle": "Security and retention",
  "charterRetentionBody": "Reports waiting to be sent are stored encrypted on your phone. On the platform, data is kept only as long as needed to handle the emergency and to meet legal obligations, and is accessible only to authorised staff.",
  "charterLiabilityTitle": "Responsibility for false reports",
  "charterLiabilityBody": "Every report mobilises rescue teams that may be needed elsewhere. Knowingly making a false report or a false alert engages your legal liability and exposes you to prosecution under Tunisian law.",
  "charterCheckbox": "I have read and accept the charter, and I understand that a knowingly false report engages my legal liability.",
